<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>{{title}} - Tellngrow</title>
  <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
</head>
<body class="bg-gray-100 min-h-screen">
  {{> sidebar}}
  
  <nav class="bg-white shadow-md p-4">
    <div class="container mx-auto flex justify-between items-center">
      <div class="flex items-center space-x-4">
        <button onclick="openSidebar()" class="text-gray-700 hover:text-purple-600 focus:outline-none">
          <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h16"></path>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-purple-600">🌱 Tellngrow</h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <div class="container mx-auto p-6 max-w-4xl">
    <!-- Back Button -->
    <a href="/reading" class="inline-flex items-center text-purple-600 hover:text-purple-700 mb-6">
      <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
      </svg>
      Back to Reading Materials
    </a>

    <!-- Article Content -->
    <article class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-lg p-8">
      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <span class="text-xs bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Mental Health</span>
          <span class="text-sm text-gray-500">5 min read</span>
          <span class="text-sm text-gray-500">•</span>
          <span class="text-sm text-gray-500">Updated: Feb 25, 2026</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4">Understanding Anxiety</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-600">A comprehensive guide to recognizing and managing anxiety in daily life.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Featured Image -->
      <div class="h-64 bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-500 to-cyan-500 rounded-lg mb-8 flex items-center justify-center">
        <span class="text-8xl">🧠</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Article Body -->
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-8 mb-4">What is Anxiety?</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Anxiety is a natural response to stress and can be beneficial in some situations. It can alert us to dangers and help us prepare and pay attention. However, anxiety disorders differ from normal feelings of nervousness or anxiousness and involve excessive fear or anxiety.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-8 mb-4">Common Symptoms</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 space-y-2 mb-4">
          <li>Feeling nervous, restless, or tense</li>
          <li>Having a sense of impending danger, panic, or doom</li>
          <li>Increased heart rate</li>
          <li>Rapid breathing (hyperventilation)</li>
          <li>Sweating and trembling</li>
          <li>Feeling weak or tired</li>
          <li>Trouble concentrating or thinking about anything other than the present worry</li>
          <li>Having trouble sleeping</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-8 mb-4">Coping Strategies</h2>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">1. Deep Breathing Exercises</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Practice deep breathing techniques to calm your nervous system. Try the 4-7-8 technique: breathe in for 4 counts, hold for 7 counts, and exhale for 8 counts.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">2. Regular Exercise</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Physical activity can help reduce anxiety symptoms. Aim for at least 30 minutes of moderate exercise most days of the week.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">3. Mindfulness and Meditation</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Practicing mindfulness can help you stay grounded in the present moment and reduce anxious thoughts about the future.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">4. Limit Caffeine and Alcohol</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Both substances can trigger or worsen anxiety. Consider reducing your intake or eliminating them entirely.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mt-6 mb-3">5. Get Enough Sleep</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Lack of sleep can exacerbate anxiety symptoms. Aim for 7-9 hours of quality sleep each night.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-8 mb-4">When to Seek Professional Help</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          If anxiety is interfering with your daily life, relationships, or work, it's important to seek help from a mental health professional. They can provide:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 space-y-2 mb-4">
          <li>Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT)</li>
          <li>Medication management if needed</li>
          <li>Personalized coping strategies</li>
          <li>Support and guidance</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-500 p-6 my-8">
          <p class="text-blue-900 font-semibold mb-2">💡 Remember:</p>
          <p class="text-blue-800">
            Anxiety is treatable, and with the right support and strategies, you can manage your symptoms and improve your quality of life. You're not alone in this journey.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mt-8 mb-4">Additional Resources</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 space-y-2 mb-4">
          <li>National Alliance on Mental Illness (NAMI): 1-800-950-NAMI</li>
          <li>Anxiety and Depression Association of America (ADAA)</li>
          <li>Crisis Text Line: Text HOME to 741741</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Related Articles -->
      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-6">Related Articles</h3>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <a href="/reading/mindfulness-meditation" class="block p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-100 transition">
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">🧘 Mindfulness Meditation</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Discover the benefits of mindfulness practice</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/reading/managing-depression" class="block p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-100 transition">
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">💭 Managing Depression</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Understanding and coping with depression</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
